WEBVTT

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:04.790
Inazuma Eleven GO is about to start!

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:07.230
Kariya dives in!

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:12.390
I won't let you have it!

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:13.930
Kariya doesn't make it!

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:15.850
The ball is in front of Minamisawa!

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:17.420
I won't let you!

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:20.950
There! Is that good enough for you?

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.060
All right!

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:23.160
Tenma!

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:24.420
Okay!

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.030
They broke past Tactics Cycle!

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:29.840
Kariya and Kirino make a magnificent combo play!

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:31.170
This'll finish it!

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:48.920
Demon God Pegasus!

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.730
Go!

00:00:55.810 --> 00:01:01.430
A shoot like that will not get past my Avatar Gigantes!

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:04.460
Gigantic Bomb!

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:19.340
It's in!

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:23.020
Matsukaze's shoot ties the score for Raimon!

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:24.270
All right!

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:28.980
Yes, now we're back on even ground!

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:31.140
Tenma!

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:41.660
Hyoudou's Avatar was beaten...

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:44.760
See that, Minamisawa?

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:47.010
That's our soccer!

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:51.160
What's this about "our soccer"?

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:54.960
I will never accept your soccer!

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:35.460
The first match in Holy Road's Nationals tournament!

00:03:35.460 --> 00:03:42.330
In the second half of Raimon versus Gassan Kunimitsu, Matsukaze's shoot ties the score at 2-2!

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:46.950
Who will make their third point, Raimon or Gassan Kunimitsu?!

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:49.910
Gassan Kunimitsu resumes the match with their kickoff!

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:53.900
Shibata!

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:57.160
Will Gassan Kunimitsu connect their pass to Minamisawa?

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:00.260
But Kurama steals the ball!

00:04:00.260 --> 00:04:01.420
Too slow!

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:02.170
Kurama!

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:03.460
Tsukishima!

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:09.780
Move up, Hamano!

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:12.810
Now with the score tied, Raimon surges forward for the attack!

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:14.170
Hamano gets past!

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:17.420
He flopped against a dribble like that?

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:20.620
It's impossible. How can our power not withstand?

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:30.980
Don't tell me that after seeing Tactics Cycle and Hyoudou's Avatar beaten, they're...

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:35.160
The fragility of administrated soccer has come to light.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:36.470
Fragility?

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:37.420
Yeah.

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:40.640
Gassan Kunimitsu is a strong team, there's no mistaking that.

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:41.300
But...

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:48.220
By only playing games according to Fifth Sector's orders, they have never faced any real hardship.

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:50.690
And now they have!

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:53.750
So that's why Gassan Kunimitsu is moving slower.

00:04:54.070 --> 00:04:58.270
A team's real worth is known upon seeing how they act in the face of adversity.

00:04:59.510 --> 00:05:01.780
We can win this game!

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:04.140
Yeah, as long as this keeps up.

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:08.490
If it's come to this, our next move...

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:11.200
It's no good.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:14.680
If I rely on these guys, we won't win a game that we <i>can</i>  win!

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:15.550
Hamano!

00:05:16.450 --> 00:05:16.910
There!

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:19.130
All right! He's totally free!

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:24.920
Minamisawa cuts for the ball!

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:30.450
I'll fight this game all on my own if I have to!

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:32.430
Kurama! Tenma!

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:34.480
Kurama and Matsukaze move in to stop him!

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:36.690
Just try and stop me if you can!

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:39.190
He gets through!

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:40.690
I'll stop you!

00:05:40.760 --> 00:05:44.610
Viva! The Great Wall Of China!

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.850
Amagi stops him in his tracks!

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:52.430
I won't let you!

00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:54.930
Minamisawa chases after him without pause!

00:05:56.570 --> 00:05:59.250
Minamisawa steals back the ball with a sliding!

00:05:59.870 --> 00:06:01.820
Now with a heading!

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:05.110
Minamisawa bodily protects the ball!

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:08.880
I can't afford to lose this game!

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:11.590
If I lose, my reason for quitting Raimon would mean nothing!

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:15.600
Those are the plays of that cool-as-a-cucumber Minamisawa-san...

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.310
Minamisawa...

00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:26.850
Osafune!

00:06:26.850 --> 00:06:27.690
Yeah!

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:36.040
Twin Mixer!

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:43.960
Minamisawa, we shall fight with you!

00:06:44.190 --> 00:06:46.730
Your plays have opened our eyes!

00:06:48.410 --> 00:06:49.620
Osafune...

00:06:49.620 --> 00:06:50.720
Kanehira...

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:54.440
Men! We'll win this game at all costs!

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:55.040
Roger!

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:56.460
Guys...

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:59.100
Move up!

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:02.900
I won't let you!

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:06.730
Masamune!

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:10.470
This time it's Gassan Kunimitsu's turn to strike back!

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:11.720
What's going on?

00:07:11.720 --> 00:07:13.780
Their agility suddenly came back!

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:15.000
It's Minamisawa.

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:18.580
His plays have unified the team.

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:21.250
Minamisawa-san's plays?

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:27.120
Minamisawa... I will not let your efforts be in vain!

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:29.250
We can win this match!

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:30.870
Hayami!

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:34.690
Hayami steals back the ball!

00:07:34.690 --> 00:07:36.580
This has turned into an incredible game!

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:39.540
Neither side is giving in! The score stands at 2-2!

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:41.680
Our attacks keep getting stopped.

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:43.650
Coach, what are your orders?

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:45.300
There are no orders.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:47.680
But at this rate...!

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:52.710
Do you not see what is happening before you?

00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:56.760
I will not lose this game!

00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:59.160
We <i>will</i>  win!

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:01.290
Bring it!

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:03.110
Endou...

00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:04.130
Yeah.

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:07.000
Their desire to win is making both teams strike each other at full force.

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:09.210
<i>This</i>  is soccer!

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:10.740
You're not getting by me!

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:14.820
Captain!

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:17.050
Kobayakawa!

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:21.250
Hamano-senpai!

00:08:21.250 --> 00:08:22.240
Kirino!

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:30.750
Twin Mixer!

00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:33.600
Kirino!

00:08:34.090 --> 00:08:37.310
This evenly matched game continues as each side advances and retreats like a wave!

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:39.280
Only minutes remain!

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:43.990
Who will score first, Gassan Kunimitsu or Raimon?!

00:08:44.480 --> 00:08:46.000
I'm counting on you, guys!

00:08:47.970 --> 00:08:49.980
Here, Kariya slips past!

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:51.370
Kai! Tsukishima!

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:54.490
Two of Gassan Kunimitsu dive in to stop him!

00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:59.140
He evades them!

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:00.370
Good one, Kariya!

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:02.890
Will Kariya be the one to make the shoot?!

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:05.050
I won't let him go any further!

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:07.080
No, he's gonna be stopped!

00:09:07.430 --> 00:09:08.260
Kariya!

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:22.370
Raimon makes their pass to Tsurugi!

00:09:30.400 --> 00:09:32.610
Sword Saint Lancelot!

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:35.720
I will protect this goal!

00:09:38.730 --> 00:09:41.390
Giant God Gigantes!

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:49.000
12.23. Inazuma Eleven GO!

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:49.890
Inazuma Eleven GO the Movie: The Ultimate Bonds, Gryphon 
 Opening Day - Friday

00:10:50.570 --> 00:10:53.760
12.23. Inazuma Eleven GO!

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:03.390
Lost Angel!

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:09.040
Gigantic Bomb!

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:24.270
Go, Lancelot!

00:11:27.170 --> 00:11:28.930
It's in!

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:32.980
There's the end game whistle!

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:35.320
Raimon makes a last-minute victory!

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:38.960
They beat Gassan Kunimitsu at 3-2!

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:40.950
Yes! Yes!

00:11:52.430 --> 00:11:53.310
Endou!

00:11:53.310 --> 00:11:54.040
Yeah!

00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:56.270
We lost...

00:11:58.640 --> 00:12:00.060
Raise your heads!

00:12:02.410 --> 00:12:04.540
You have lost a game...

00:12:04.540 --> 00:12:06.830
But you gave it your all.

00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:11.610
Today, you have faced soccer with all of your worth for the first time...

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:14.260
...by putting everything you had into the ball.

00:12:14.930 --> 00:12:16.180
Everything I had...

00:12:27.590 --> 00:12:32.350
Thanks to you, I too have remembered a soccer I had once forgotten.

00:12:33.750 --> 00:12:34.740
Coach...

00:12:49.170 --> 00:12:51.450
For me to realize it now after all this time...

00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:53.870
Shindou.

00:12:54.270 --> 00:12:58.080
I finally understand what you guys were trying to do.

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:00.300
Minamisawa-san...

00:13:06.490 --> 00:13:08.170
Keep doing your best...

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:09.720
Tenma!

00:13:14.930 --> 00:13:15.940
Okay!

00:13:19.820 --> 00:13:21.120
Minamisawa-san!

00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:27.360
Gassan Kunimitsu might need someone like you on their side...

00:13:27.970 --> 00:13:31.530
But we'll always be waiting.

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:41.490
Thank you.

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:43.800
Let's go.

00:13:46.920 --> 00:13:54.520
Within the thunderous applause praising them for their strenuous efforts, Gassan Kunimitsu leaves Cyclone Stadium!

00:13:56.640 --> 00:14:00.570
We can't go back to Fifth Sector now...

00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:05.840
What's with them...

00:14:05.840 --> 00:14:07.820
I thought they were squabbling among friends.

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:09.110
Kariya.

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:11.530
Thank you for trusting me.

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:13.110
Trusting you?

00:14:13.530 --> 00:14:15.790
I wasn't trusting you.

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:17.560
I know.

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:21.000
You wanted to win and that was it.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:25.090
But I can tell how much you like soccer.

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:29.520
Are you sure you should be saying that?

00:14:29.520 --> 00:14:31.010
I'm a Seed.

00:14:31.010 --> 00:14:33.300
There's no telling what I'll do next.

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:35.720
You're not a Seed.

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:42.510
Don't blame me if you regret it later.

00:14:58.600 --> 00:15:00.330
You're here already?

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:02.000
Sorry to keep you waiting...

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:03.880
Coach Hitomiko.

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:10.130
I'm sorry for putting Kariya-kun in your care so suddenly, Endou-kun.

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:14.550
No, a soccer freak like him is more than welcome here.

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:19.320
He's snide, but the ball he kicks is a gentle one.

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:23.360
I can tell how kindhearted he is through the ball.

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:28.910
He was eleven when he first arrived at Sun Garden.

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:35.590
Please take good care of him.

00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:41.620
His father was tricked and pressured into bankruptcy.

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:45.420
Seeing that caused him to stop trusting others.

00:15:45.420 --> 00:15:47.370
He wouldn't fit in with anyone.

00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:51.590
But he seemed to like soccer.

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:54.180
I'd always see him kicking the ball all by himself.

00:15:56.870 --> 00:15:58.680
He'll be fine.

00:15:59.030 --> 00:16:02.320
Kariya has friends now who will support him.

00:16:05.090 --> 00:16:05.940
Yeah.

00:16:06.890 --> 00:16:08.660
That's Raimon.

00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:14.160
I'm back, Sasuke.

00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:16.580
Welcome back.

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:17.460
I'm home!

00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:20.290
Oh, is this a new friend?

00:16:20.710 --> 00:16:22.820
You must be Kariya Masaki-kun!

00:16:22.820 --> 00:16:23.290
Yes.

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:25.750
Tenma's told me so much about you.

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:28.390
I thought we could all celebrate together our win today.

00:16:28.390 --> 00:16:29.160
I see.

00:16:29.490 --> 00:16:31.090
Well, come on in.

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:32.170
Excuse my intrusion.

00:16:33.770 --> 00:16:36.400
Then Captain got the ball!

00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:38.080
That was so cool!

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:39.840
I totally thought he got the slip!

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:43.980
Really? Well, I knew that Captain would be good enough to stop him.

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:45.780
Yeah, right!

00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:46.600
What?

00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:49.570
Do these guys always hang out together like this?

00:16:49.570 --> 00:16:51.710
Kariya-kun, would you like another piece?

00:16:51.710 --> 00:16:53.390
Yes, thank you!

00:16:54.760 --> 00:16:58.800
I have to keep practicing more and more so I can be like Captain and the others.

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:01.330
Then I'll work hard too and make a hissatsu technique!

00:17:02.820 --> 00:17:06.180
I'm a defender, but all I have is Full Throttle Jump.

00:17:06.180 --> 00:17:08.570
I don't have any defense hissatsu techniques.

00:17:08.570 --> 00:17:10.720
A defense hissatsu technique, huh?

00:17:10.720 --> 00:17:14.110
Since you're gonna do it, why not make it a two-person technique?

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:16.050
Two-person technique?

00:17:16.050 --> 00:17:18.950
Like, maybe Tenma-kun could kick Shinsuke-kun up in the air or something.

00:17:18.950 --> 00:17:21.470
Me, kick Shinsuke up in the air?

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:23.640
Tenma!

00:17:27.470 --> 00:17:28.680
All right!

00:17:31.510 --> 00:17:33.150
That's a great idea!

00:17:33.150 --> 00:17:36.150
That'll make the best use of Shinsuke's jumping ability!

00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:37.230
Yeah!

00:17:37.230 --> 00:17:40.090
Then you'll start practicing for that tomorrow, right?

00:17:40.090 --> 00:17:40.700
Yeah!

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:45.200
There's no way it'll work, idiots.

00:17:45.570 --> 00:17:47.810
So, what are you going to name it?

00:17:47.810 --> 00:17:51.070
Since Tenma is kicking, how about Soyokaze Jump?

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:53.780
Nah, that sounds too normal.

00:17:54.680 --> 00:17:56.780
It's not normal at all.

00:17:56.780 --> 00:17:58.790
Then how about Rocket Jump?

00:17:58.790 --> 00:17:59.840
Not that either.

00:17:59.840 --> 00:18:01.050
Rocket Defense?

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:02.490
Could be better.

00:18:02.490 --> 00:18:04.520
Then what?

00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:08.430
Do you have any ideas, Kariya?

00:18:08.840 --> 00:18:09.640
Me?

00:18:11.260 --> 00:18:13.280
Since you're jumping with a bang...

00:18:13.810 --> 00:18:15.490
How about Kaboom Jump?

00:18:20.430 --> 00:18:22.090
Lame!

00:18:22.090 --> 00:18:25.240
Y-You guys are the ones who asked me for my opinion!

00:18:25.240 --> 00:18:27.390
But Kaboom Jump?

00:18:27.390 --> 00:18:29.030
That's just lame!

00:18:29.030 --> 00:18:31.420
So lame! Definitely no way!

00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:37.130
Bad news?

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:38.400
Yes, sir.

00:18:38.400 --> 00:18:42.100
Some schools are beginning to raise a revolt against you.

00:18:42.460 --> 00:18:45.780
Hibiki has gained their votes against our expectations.

00:18:45.780 --> 00:18:49.310
I believe that Raimon's continuous victories are influencing them...

00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:52.050
Then we'll just have to nip it in the bud.

00:18:52.050 --> 00:18:53.450
Use any means necessary.

00:18:53.450 --> 00:18:55.070
Destroy Raimon.

00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:56.540
Yes, sir.

00:18:58.270 --> 00:19:01.370
Someone is here asking to see you, sir.

00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:06.070
I've brought him.

00:19:06.780 --> 00:19:07.880
Good work.

00:19:12.090 --> 00:19:13.670
Endou Mamoru.

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:15.000
I thought you would come.

00:19:16.550 --> 00:19:18.050
Gouenji...

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:20.090
So it was you.

00:19:20.570 --> 00:19:21.850
Why?

00:19:21.850 --> 00:19:24.390
Why are you a part of Fifth Sector?!

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:26.900
Gouenji!

00:19:26.900 --> 00:19:29.100
I am not Gouenji.

00:19:29.920 --> 00:19:32.290
I am Ishido Shuuji.

00:19:36.200 --> 00:19:38.830
What happened to you?

00:19:38.830 --> 00:19:41.890
Why are you doing this and taking soccer away from everyone?

00:19:41.890 --> 00:19:46.110
You ought to know more than anyone in the world how painful it feels not being able to play soccer!

00:19:46.110 --> 00:19:49.160
So why... Why are you administrating soccer?!

00:19:51.870 --> 00:19:53.480
Stop this.

00:19:53.480 --> 00:20:00.020
Instead of continuing this stupid fight, come think with me about how to bring back the old soccer!

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:03.750
If we all think together, I'm sure we'll find an answer!

00:20:03.750 --> 00:20:05.180
Don't you get it?

00:20:05.670 --> 00:20:07.850
Soccer has changed.

00:20:10.570 --> 00:20:13.090
It won't return to the way it's been.

00:20:13.090 --> 00:20:18.360
Therefore, I must control soccer and divide it equally amongst everyone.

00:20:19.290 --> 00:20:20.820
Gouenji...

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:23.240
There is nothing left to talk about.

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:24.230
Leave.

00:20:36.180 --> 00:20:37.260
I see...

00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:38.740
Gouenji-kun...

00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:45.300
I just can't believe he would say something like that...

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:48.740
But you want to take it back, don't you?

00:20:49.300 --> 00:20:50.860
The old soccer.

00:20:53.130 --> 00:20:55.690
Then you'll just have to do it.

00:20:56.490 --> 00:20:59.720
Despite what's happening, you press on the path that you believe in.

00:20:59.720 --> 00:21:01.450
That's Endou-kun.

00:21:02.640 --> 00:21:06.310
I just know your feelings will reach Gouenji-kun one day.

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:08.280
Natsumi...

00:21:08.610 --> 00:21:10.550
Now, let's have dinner!

00:21:11.180 --> 00:21:15.300
I made well-stewed hamburger just for you today.

00:21:15.300 --> 00:21:16.740
Let's eat.

00:21:21.430 --> 00:21:23.900
How is it? I didn't cook it for too long, did I?

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:30.810
I-I think it's perfect.

00:21:30.810 --> 00:21:32.430
Thank goodness!

00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:35.890
This is my first time making stewed hamburger, so I was worried.

00:21:36.510 --> 00:21:38.630
As long as I think it tastes good, it'll work out somehow.

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:42.540
As long as I think it tastes good, it'll work out somehow...

00:21:45.410 --> 00:21:46.960
You looking to join?

00:21:46.960 --> 00:21:47.850
Yes!

00:21:47.850 --> 00:21:49.790
I want to join the soccer club!

00:21:50.440 --> 00:21:52.310
I like your enthusiasm!

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:53.680
What's your name?

00:21:53.990 --> 00:21:54.860
It's Hikaru!

00:21:55.320 --> 00:21:56.520
Hikaru-kun, is it?

00:21:56.520 --> 00:21:57.750
And your surname?

00:21:57.750 --> 00:21:59.020
Surname...

00:21:59.020 --> 00:22:01.250
Um... well...

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:04.230
That is... um...

00:22:04.230 --> 00:22:06.220
Well... u-um...

00:22:10.040 --> 00:22:11.970
K-Kageyama.

00:22:12.440 --> 00:22:13.990
I'm Kageyama Hikaru!

00:22:20.380 --> 00:22:21.110
Ka...

00:22:22.340 --> 00:22:23.780
Kageyama?!

00:23:54.600 --> 00:23:59.040
As the Raimon Eleven ride its wave, another new member appears!

00:23:59.250 --> 00:24:03.330
Next on Inazuma Eleven GO, 
 He's Back!

00:24:03.580 --> 00:24:05.380
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:24:14.890 --> 00:24:17.890
The Inazuma Eleven GO's proverb today is...

00:24:22.200 --> 00:24:26.040
A team's real worth is known upon seeing how they act in the face of adversity!

00:24:26.040 --> 00:24:26.700
That's all!
